# Line endings.
#
# Shell scripts and CI workflows MUST be LF. This is not a style preference: on a Windows
# checkout these files get CRLF, and bash then reads a line continuation as backslash-CR
# rather than backslash-newline. The backslash escapes the carriage return, the command breaks
# apart, and the arguments after it are passed as garbage.
#
# That exact failure took the first CI run of this repository red: a `git commit \` continuation
# became `git commit` followed by a literal `n`, and git answered
# "error: pathspec 'n' did not match any file(s) known to git". The build, the packaging and the
# release notes had all succeeded; only the last step broke, and it skipped the publish.
*.sh            text eol=lf
*.bash          text eol=lf
.github/**/*.yml  text eol=lf
.github/**/*.yaml text eol=lf

# Fonts and icons are binary. Never let Git rewrite bytes inside them — a "text" font file is
# a corrupt font file, and it fails silently as a fallback rather than as an error.
*.woff2  binary
*.woff   binary
*.ico    binary
*.png    binary
*.jpg    binary
*.exe    binary
*.nupkg  binary
